  "text": "A woman of the old Irish tales named Caolainn belongs to a healing well in County Roscommon. The tradition says that at this place she mended a wound she had dealt to herself. When a man praised the loveliness of her eyes, she gouged them out and hurled them at him. Then, guiding herself by touch, she found the well, pulled up the rushes that ringed it, and wiped the blood from her emptied eye pits, whereupon her sight came back. The tale was repeated about the saint Brigit, and the wells blessed to her were likewise said to cure ailments of the eyes.",
